<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Subsequent annual wellness visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a personalized prevention plan given in braille and accessible electronic text. Depression and alcohol screens are negative. Cognition is intact by direct observation and a tactile word-recall check, done the same way as at the March baseline. [S]<list><item>Next annual wellness visit in one year, double length, with a qualified tactile interpreter booked by the clinic.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Fall risk, reduced (Z91.81)</content>. No falls in seven months; Timed Up and Go 11.0 seconds. [S]<list><item>Continue daily strength and balance exercises.</item><item>Repeat the STEADI screen at next year&apos;s wellness visit, or sooner after any fall.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Lifelong blindness (H54.0X55)</content>. Socket and prosthesis healthy. [S]<list><item>Yearly ocularist visit to polish the prosthesis, due next month.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Lifelong profound deafness (H91.93)</content>. Communication by tactile fingerspelling, speech, and braille works well for her. She is not interested in evaluation for hearing technology, and that choice is respected. [S]<list><item>Keep the communication access plan and hospital passport current.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, this season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>High-dose vaccine given today</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, this season</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended at her age; booked at the clinic next week, with an interpreter</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PCV20 about two and a half years ago; no further doses needed</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Single dose two years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Two-dose series completed about three and a half years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap about seven years ago; next due in about three years</td></tr><tr><td>Bone density (DXA)</td><td>Up to date</td><td>In March: femoral neck T-score -1.9, below the FRAX treatment thresholds; repeat in about two years or sooner if risk changes</td></tr><tr><td>Falls prevention</td><td>Completed today</td><td>STEADI screen negative for new falls; exercise program continues</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 score 1 in braille</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol misuse screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 2</td></tr><tr><td>Cognitive assessment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Direct observation and a tactile word-recall check (three of three words); standard tools rely on vision or hearing and are not used</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>126/74 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time antibody test for adults 18 to 79, with her consent</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time triple panel, with her consent</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Declined</td><td>Normal colonoscopy about eight years ago; at 79 screening is an individual decision, and after discussion she chose to stop</td></tr><tr><td>Breast cancer screening</td><td>Declined</td><td>Evidence is insufficient after 74; after discussion she chose to stop mammograms</td></tr><tr><td>Cervical cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not recommended after 65 with adequate prior screening</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer and abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never smoker</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Lifelong deafblindness; communication and sensory needs are reviewed instead</td></tr><tr><td>Ocular prosthesis care</td><td>Due</td><td>Yearly ocularist polishing due next month</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: High-dose influenza vaccine, 1959-1960 season [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Zhou SY, et al. Training Medical Students in Deaf, DeafBlind, and Hard-of-Hearing Patient Care Through Interactive Lecture and Simulation. MedEdPORTAL 2025;21:11566 (2025); Medicare Wellness Visits (Medicare Learning Network) (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Hepatitis C and hepatitis B results will be sent in braille. COVID-19 vaccine next week. Ocularist next month. Next annual wellness visit in one year. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
