<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.21" extension="2015-08-01"/>
    <code code="42348-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Advance directives"/>
    <title>Advance Care Planning</title>
    <text><paragraph>Voluntary advance care planning discussion of about 25 minutes, with her consent, through a qualified tactile interpreter. She has a written health care directive in braille and print and has named a long-time friend as her health care agent; a copy is now in the chart. She wants full treatment for any illness from which she could recover. She would not want prolonged mechanical ventilation or tube feeding if she could no longer communicate by touch or speech and recovery of communication were improbable. Her hospital communication passport, attached to the directive, explains that she receives language by fingerspelling into her hand, speaks for herself, needs a qualified tactile interpreter for any consent or serious discussion, and asks to be touched on the hand to signal presence before any care. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
